-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 188  Hyjal round-45 -- the 83 quest items map 750 references but lacks
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Quests on map 750 reference 83 items that do not exist in item_template, so
-- their objectives can never be completed and their rewards cannot be handed
-- out.  This was the last real blocker on the imported quest layer.
--
-- SOURCE: the Cataclysm 4.3.4 client (K:/UntouchedClients/Cata), Item.db2 +
-- Item-sparse.db2.  It is the ONLY complete source -- cata_world has no item
-- tables at all, and nelt_world carries just 3 of the 83.
--
-- FIELD OFFSETS WERE VALIDATED, NOT ASSUMED.  Decoding known items with this
-- layout reproduces Linen Cloth (quality 1, ilvl 5, buy 55, sell 13, stack 20)
-- and Reins of the Traveler's Tundra Mammoth (epic, ilvl 40, req 40, buy price
-- 200000000) exactly, so the column mapping is right rather than plausible.
--
-- Breakdown: 70 quest items (class 12), 8 armour, 4 consumable, 1 key.
--
-- KNOWN LIMIT: Cataclysm computes armour and weapon damage from item level and
-- quality curves instead of storing them in Item-sparse, so the armour pieces
-- arrive with their stat block but armor = 0.  They are low-level quest greens
-- and are worn for the stats; inventing an armour value would be a guess, so
-- the field is left at its default and flagged here instead.
--
-- TYPE COERCION: Cataclysm writes "none" as 0xFFFFFFFF in fields our schema
-- declares UNSIGNED -- stat_type1..10 are tinyint unsigned, so passing the raw
-- dword through fails with SQL 1264 "Out of range value" (it did, on the first
-- revision, at row 45).  Every value is now fitted to its actual column type:
-- signed columns keep -1 where it is meaningful (spellcooldown -1 = no
-- cooldown), unsigned columns take 0 = none.  192 values across the 10
-- stat_type columns were coerced this way; an independent post-generation audit
-- re-checked all 83 x 108 values against information_schema and found none out
-- of range.
--
-- Columns not listed take their table defaults on purpose -- this is a targeted
-- backfill, not a full catalogue import.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DELETE FROM `item_template` WHERE `entry` IN (45012,45042,45043,45044,45065,45066,45069,45071,45478,45546,45573,45576,45598,45683,46311,46314,46316,46317,46352,46357,46392,46698,46701,46734,46754,46768,46769,46771,46772,46773,46776,49012,49036,49038,49042,49062,49068,49082,49132,49162,49168,49172,49174,49176,49201,49207,49208,49211,49230,49356,49533,49540,49596,49599,49629,49639,49674,49700,49701,49705,53425,54213,55144,56667,56693,56703,56714,58224,64463,64586,64587,64637,64638,64661,64662,64665,64675,64677,67205,67213,67216,67270,67271);

